<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 216 0 R/E<>/Pg 19 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

374 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 216 0 R/E(Language and Formatting: We make our copy more casual and conversational in terms of word choice, language, grammar, etc. We don\220t use medical jargon when communicating with our clients. Instead, we use simpler terms to make our content easier to read and follow. We will use some minor slang, nothing too crazy. When writing posts, we do use the oxford comma. When considering dates and times, we write the month out and then use the number keys to denote the date. Time we write out the full time, for example, we would say 4:00 pm. When it comes to the length of captions, we are usually on the longer side. Almost always does. The \215see more\216 option comes up, but it's only a few lines more after that button is clicked. )/Pg 19 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

375 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 216 0 R/E(Glossary: Because of the use of simple language, we need to define any terms. All employees know the general terms such as wellness exam, preventive care, etc. )/Pg 19 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

